      "seed": 221901516,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3345186,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795365707110,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Registry SELECTs records by (kind,id), INSERTs version 1, and UPDATEs only when the expected version matches.\nArtifact INSERT uses a SHA-256 content ID. Budget reservations lock the budget row FOR UPDATE.\nreservations, reservation_values and settlements track idempotent model usage by workflow and call.\nRole schemas persist TASK, TASK_MESSAGE and MODEL_CALL records plus result artifacts.\nPostgreSQL advisory locks guard service and migration ownership. Schema selection is set at JVM startup.\nLegacy unscoped routes can forward through Simulation to Feedback or Personalization over analyst REST.\nSimulation also forwards the legacy outcome event path with the dedicated outcomes credential.\nBank binding lives in process configuration: bank-local owner URLs, database URL, policies and token files.",
      "originalText": "Registry SELECTs records by (kind,id), INSERTs version 1, and UPDATEs only when the expected version matches.\nArtifact INSERT uses a SHA-256 content ID. Budget reservations lock the budget row FOR UPDATE.\nreservations, reservation_values and settlements track idempotent model usage by workflow and call.\nRole schemas persist TASK, TASK_MESSAGE and MODEL_CALL records plus result artifacts.\nPostgreSQL advisory locks guard service and migration ownership. Schema selection is set at JVM startup.\nLegacy unscoped routes can forward through Simulation to Feedback or Personalization over analyst REST.\nSimulation also forwards the legacy outcome event path with the dedicated outcomes credential.\nBank binding lives in process configuration: bank-local owner URLs, database URL, policies and token files.",
      "fontSize": 21,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true
    },
